
### unseal against the vault file on disk
$ vaultctl unseal /tmp/kvdemo.vault
using the KDF parameters from /tmp/kvdemo.vault (2 secrets, 200000 iterations)
unsealed (2 secrets, auto-lock in 300s)

$ vaultctl seal
sealed; key wiped from kernel memory


### now a wrong passphrase, three times
$ vaultctl unseal /tmp/kvdemo.vault        # attempt 1
vaultctl: KVAULT_UNSEAL: Permission denied
state: SEALED failed_attempts: 1/3 
$ vaultctl unseal /tmp/kvdemo.vault        # attempt 2
vaultctl: KVAULT_UNSEAL: Permission denied
state: SEALED failed_attempts: 2/3 
$ vaultctl unseal /tmp/kvdemo.vault        # attempt 3
vaultctl: KVAULT_UNSEAL: Permission denied
state: LOCKED_OUT failed_attempts: 3/3 


### and now the CORRECT passphrase is refused too
$ vaultctl unseal /tmp/kvdemo.vault
vaultctl: KVAULT_UNSEAL: Resource temporarily unavailable

$ sleep 6     # lockout_secs=5
$ vaultctl unseal /tmp/kvdemo.vault
using the KDF parameters from /tmp/kvdemo.vault (2 secrets, 200000 iterations)
unsealed (2 secrets, auto-lock in 300s)
